<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Tylis</h1><p class="st-meta">277 BCE – 212 BCE (approx.) · capital Tylis</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Celtic kingdom in eastern Thrace that extorted heavy tribute from Byzantium after the great Celtic invasion of 279 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/celts">Celts</a> who had invaded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a> in 279 BCE, defeating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a>, settled in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a> under their leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comontorius">Comontorius</a> around 277 BCE. They founded a kingdom with its capital at Tylis, whose exact location near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkan-mountains">Haemus</a> or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strandzha">Strandzha</a> mountains is still debated.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kingdom lived largely from tribute. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polybius">Polybius</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantium">Byzantium</a> paid it ever larger sums, rising to 80 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/talent">talents</a> a year. Celtic warriors ruled over a Thracian population, and coins of the last king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cavarus">Cavarus</a>, are known. Cavarus was praised as a statesman and mediated in the war between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/rhodes">Rhodes</a> in 220 BCE.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 212 BCE the local <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thracians">Thracians</a> rose against Celtic rule and destroyed the kingdom. Thracian dynasts reasserted themselves in the region, which later came under Macedonian and Roman influence.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 277 BCE – 212 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Balkans and Hungary</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:54.19%;width:1.29%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>277 BCE – 212 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tylis</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Comontorius, Cavarus</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish (Celtic)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tylis, Celtic kingdom of Tylis</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-244&amp;focus=kingdom-of-tylis" aria-label="Kingdom of Tylis on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5299 664 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Tylis lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5619 920h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5619 920h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Tylis. <a href="/atlas?year=-244&amp;focus=kingdom-of-tylis">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

